{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"title":"Systems","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"Systems"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"],"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemParameter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents"],"anchor":"System-Parameters","title":"System Parameters"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity"],"anchor":"Building-and-Running-Schedules","title":"Building and Running Schedules"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem"],"anchor":"Main-Actor-Systems","title":"Main-Actor Systems"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges"],"anchor":"Built-In-Systems","title":"Built-In Systems"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming"],"anchor":"Profiling","title":"Profiling"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A world holds data: entities and their components, and resources. A "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"system"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" holds a rule: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"step that reads part of the world and changes part of it, such as “every entity with a velocity"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"moves” or “gravity pulls on everything that isn’t frozen.” A "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"schedule"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the systems of one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"frame or step and runs them on a world, each once per run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The examples throughout this module use these components, resources and event:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct Position: Component { var x: Double, y: Double }","struct Velocity: Component { var dx: Double, dy: Double }","struct Health: Component { var current: Int }","struct Frozen: Component {}","","struct Score: Resource { var points: Int }","struct TimeStep: Resource { var seconds: Double }","struct Paused: Resource {}","","struct Damage: Event { var target: Entity, amount: Int }"]},{"anchor":"Declare-a-System","type":"heading","text":"Declare a System","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The simplest way to write a system is to mark a type with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"@System","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro and give it a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method. The method’s parameters say what the system works on, and their types say how:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","type":"reference"},{"text":" writes components, a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","type":"reference"},{"text":" reads them, and a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads a resource. The following two systems pull everything that isn’t frozen downward, then move","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it by its velocity:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@System","struct Gravity {","    func run(_ falling: Update<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        falling { velocity, _ in velocity.dy -= 10 }","    }","}","","@System","struct Movement {","    func run(_ movers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        movers { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx","            position.y += row.components.dy","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because the parameters’ types state what each system reads and writes, the macro writes the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access"},{"type":"text","text":" for you: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gravity"},{"type":"text","text":" writes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Velocity"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Movement"},{"type":"text","text":" writes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Velocity"},{"type":"text","text":". A schedule uses the access to decide which systems can run at the same time."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can also conform a type to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"},{"text":" by hand and write its ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)"},{"text":" method, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"receives the whole world. See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"},{"text":" for when to do that.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Run-Systems-in-a-Schedule","type":"heading","text":"Run Systems in a Schedule","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is built from a list of systems, written in a result builder. Running it runs each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system once. The following example drops a ball for one frame:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 90.0)\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems run in the order you write them, unless an ordering constraint says otherwise."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" require one system to run after or before another; "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names a group of systems so constraints can refer to all of them at once; and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"runIf(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" skips"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a system when a condition doesn’t hold."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Systems whose accesses don’t conflict, because neither writes what the other reads or writes,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run at the same time, and the world ends as though they had run one after another. Systems that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conflict run in order. When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, their order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rests only on how they happen to be written; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" finds those pairs so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"test can keep a schedule free of them.","type":"text"}]}]}],"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/MainActorSystem":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that runs on the main actor, for work that touches main-actor state such as a user"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interface."}],"type":"topic","title":"MainActorSystem","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/mainactorsystem","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MainActorSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MainActorSystem","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"type":"topic","title":"Systems","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","url":"\/documentation\/systems","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ForwardChanges":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ForwardChanges"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A system that yields each component of one type added or changed since it last ran to an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"asynchronous stream, with its entity.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/forwardchanges","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ForwardChanges"}],"role":"symbol","title":"ForwardChanges"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Ambiguity":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Ambiguity"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/ambiguity","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Two systems of a schedule whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint orders, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the order they run in rests only on the order they were written in."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Ambiguity"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Ambiguity"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/run(in:)":{"title":"run(in:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"run","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"in","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\